README_TPL = '''# {name}

An [ewe](https://github.com/prj786/ewe) desktop plugin (`{id}`).

## What ewe does, what you do

You draw and behave: every `.qml` in this repo is yours. ewe decides where
it lives and what the user can change about it:

- **bar-widget**: ewe puts it in the top bar (left / centre / right; the
  user can hide it in Settings -> Top bar). It must be an `Item` with an
  implicit size.
- **desktop-widget**: ewe places it on the desktop; the user moves it
  (Super+Shift+W, then drag), makes it sticky (above windows) or hides it.
- **panel / overlay / menu**: your own window, opened over IPC
  (`qs ipc call {id} toggle`), bindable to a key.
- **settings** in `manifest.json` become a form in Komble and arrive in
  every entry point as `settings` ({{key: value}}).

`import qs` gives you the shell's `Theme` roles (colours, radii, fonts),
`Globals` (accent, dnd, battery...) and `Log`. See docs/PLUGINS.md in ewe.

## Develop

    ewe-plugin dev .        # link this folder, enable, restart the shell, follow its log
    ewe-plugin validate .   # the manifest and entry points

## Ship

Push this repo anywhere git can reach; users install it with

    ewe-plugin add {url_hint} --enable

or from Komble -> Plugins.
'''

